CHANGELOG – php-demo / BPA-Demo
================================

All changes are listed in reverse chronological order.
Format: YYYY-MM-DD @ HH:MM  <summary>

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 17:00 - [Fix – correct PHP probe browser agent enable property name]:
  The correct INI property to enable browser agent auto-injection is
  wily_php_agent.enable.browseragent.snippet.autoInjection=1 (integer flag),
  not wily_php_agent.browseragent.autoInjection.enabled=true (boolean string).

  - src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh: browser agent block updated:
    • Enabled path: sets enable.browseragent.snippet.autoInjection=1
    • Disabled path: sets enable.browseragent.snippet.autoInjection=0
    • Both paths: remove the legacy browseragent.autoInjection.enabled line
      (whether pre-configured by the DX O2 installer or left over from a
      previous container build).
    • snippetString handling unchanged.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 16:30 - [Fix – YAML parse error from mixed environment block style]:
  Mixing mapping style (KEY: VALUE) and list style (- ITEM) in the same
  YAML environment block is illegal.  The previous fix introduced a list-form
  entry (- APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET) alongside mapping-form entries, causing:
    yaml: did not find expected key (line 91 / line 112)

  Fix: convert the entire apachephp environment block to list form.
  Hardcoded Compose-network values use (- KEY=value); all variables
  read from .config use passthrough form (- KEY), relying on compose.sh
  to export each one with a safe default.

  - docker-compose.yml: apachephp environment block rewritten as uniform
    list style.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 16:00 - [Fix – APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET not reaching container in Docker Compose]:
  Two root causes prevented the browser snippet from appearing in the
  apachephp container environment:

  1. compose.sh did not export APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET (nor the many other DX O2
     variables added since the original export block was written).  Docker Compose
     reads ${VAR:-default} from the process environment; unexported variables
     always resolved to the empty default.
  2. docker-compose.yml used the YAML-interpolation form
     (APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET: ${APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET:-}).  Because the snippet
     value contains double-quotes the substituted YAML could fail to parse.

  Fixes:
  - build-scripts/compose.sh: export block extended to include APMIA_DEPLOY,
    APMIA_HOST_NAME, APMIA_PROCESS_NAME, APMIA_PHP_AGENT_NAME, APMIA_WEB_AGENT_NAME,
    APMIA_PHP_COLLECTOR_HOST/PORT, APMIA_BTL_HOST/PORT, MYSQL_MONITOR, and
    APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET (all with correct defaults).  Also corrected
    images_present() which still referenced the old php-fpm and nginx image names
    instead of apache-php and dx-o2-agents.
  - docker-compose.yml: APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET switched to the list/passthrough
    form (- APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET) so the value reaches the container verbatim
    without YAML interpolation or special-character escaping.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 15:30 - [Fix – Browser agent auto-injection not disabled when snippet absent]:
  The DX O2 installer download may ship wily_php_agent.ini with
  browseragent.autoInjection already enabled and a default snippet value.
  The else branch in entrypoint.sh previously only logged a message but did
  not clear these pre-existing entries, causing auto-injection to remain
  active even when APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET was empty in .config.

  Fix: when APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET is unset the else branch now:
    1. Sets wily_php_agent.browseragent.autoInjection.enabled=false (if the
       property is present in the INI).
    2. Removes any wily_php_agent.browseragent.autoInjection.snippetString
       line, making .config the authoritative and exclusive control point.

  - src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh: else branch updated with explicit disable
    and scrub logic for pre-configured browser agent properties.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 15:00 - [Feat – Browser agent auto-injection via PHP probe]:
  Added opt-in browser agent JavaScript auto-injection through the PHP probe.
  When APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET is set the PHP probe writes two properties into
  wily_php_agent.ini at container startup and injects the snippet into the
  <head> of every HTML response:
    wily_php_agent.browseragent.autoInjection.enabled=true
    wily_php_agent.browseragent.autoInjection.snippetString=<value>

  The snippet string (a <script> tag referencing the DX O2 tenant URL) is
  written using printf %s to handle special characters without shell escaping.

  - src/apache-php/entrypoint.sh: added APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET variable and
    browser agent injection block inside the PHP probe section.
  - docker-compose.yml: APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET added to apachephp service.
  - helm/php-demo/values.yaml: browserSnippet field added (empty default).
  - helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml: APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET env var
    added to apache-php container when dxo2.browserSnippet is non-empty.
  - build-scripts/deploy.sh: apmia_browser_snippet wired into generate_values().
  - .config.example: APMIA_BROWSER_SNIPPET documented with instructions.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 14:00 - [Feat – APMIA_DEPLOY flag, APMENV log level, MariaDB DB Monitor]:
  Three adapations from a reference working DX O2 Docker Compose configuration:

  1. APMIA_DEPLOY flag (passive volume mode):
     When APMIA_DEPLOY=false the dxo2 container seeds the named volume with
     the agent tree but does not start the IA or BTL daemons (use with an
     external IA).  Default remains true (active mode – IA started from the
     dxo2 container).
     - src/dx-o2-agents/entrypoint.sh: added APMIA_DEPLOY check; when false,
       prints message then exec sleep infinity (keeps volume accessible).
     - docker-compose.yml, helm/values.yaml, deployment.yaml, deploy.sh: wired
       APMIA_DEPLOY throughout.

  2. Log level via APMENV_LOG4J_LOGGER_INTROSCOPEAGENT (native IA mechanism):
     Replaced the custom APMIA_LOG_LEVEL env var (unused by the IA) with
     APMENV_LOG4J_LOGGER_INTROSCOPEAGENT="<level>, logfile" which the IA agent
     startup script reads natively.  APMIA_LOG_LEVEL in .config still controls
     the level; it is now formatted into the APMENV_* value.

  3. MariaDB/MySQL DB Monitor via APMENV_INTROSCOPE_AGENT_DBMONITOR_MYSQL_*:
     The APMIA DB Monitor extension now polls the MariaDB instance using the
     MARIADB_USER / MARIADB_PASSWORD credentials from .config.
     - docker-compose.yml: dxo2 service gains MYSQL_MONITOR and twelve
       APMENV_DBMONITOR vars; hostname is the Compose service name "mariadb".
     - helm/values.yaml: added dxo2.dbMonitor section (non-sensitive defaults).
     - deployment.yaml: conditional dbMonitor block; credentials injected via
       secretKeyRef (MARIADB_USER / MARIADB_PASSWORD from the mariadb Secret).
     - deploy.sh: MYSQL_MONITOR and instanceName wired into generated values.
     - .config.example: documented APMIA_DEPLOY and MYSQL_MONITOR.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 13:00 - [Fix – Set container hostname so PHP probe and BPA report readable names]:
  The PHP probe and BPA Apache module pick up the OS hostname of the container
  they run in (apachephp / apache-php), not the DX O2 IA hostname override.
  Auto-generated Docker container IDs (e.g. ae17a0b2e78c) were appearing as
  the host segment of the metric path.

  - docker-compose.yml: added `hostname: ${APMIA_HOST_NAME:-bpa-demo-host}` to
    the apachephp service so both the PHP probe and BPA module report under a
    human-readable hostname in Compose.
  - helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml: added `hostname: dxo2.hostName`
    to the pod template spec; all containers in the pod (including apache-php)
    share this hostname, fixing the metric path for both probes.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-06-17 @ 12:30 - [Refactor – Switch DX O2 agent identity to APMENV_* native mechanism]:
  Replaced the manual IntroscopeAgent.profile patching and wrapper.conf JVM-arg
  injection with the official APMENV_* Docker container environment variable
  mechanism supported natively by the APMIA agent startup script.

  The agent reads APMENV_* vars at launch and applies them as introscope.*
  property overrides without any file modification:
    APMENV_INTROSCOPE_AGENT_AGENTNAME         → introscope.agent.agentName
    APMENV_INTROSCOPE_AGENT_APPLICATION_NAME  → introscope.agent.application.name
    APMENV_INTROSCOPE_AGENT_HOSTNAME          → introscope.agent.hostName
    APMENV_INTROSCOPE_AGENT_CUSTOMPROCESSNAME → introscope.agent.customProcessName

  - src/dx-o2-agents/entrypoint.sh: removed _set_profile_prop(), sed profile
    patching, and _add_jvm_arg()/wrapper.conf injection; replaced with four
    export APMENV_* lines that also accept legacy APMIA_* vars as a fallback.
  - docker-compose.yml: dxo2 service now sets APMENV_* keys sourced from the
    APMIA_* shell vars in .config (user-facing naming unchanged).
  - helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml: dx-o2-agent sidecar env block
    updated from APMIA_* to APMENV_* names.
  - helm/php-demo/values.yaml: agent identity comment block updated to document
    the APMENV_* convention and the property mapping.

