2026-06-16 @ 15:00 - [Add DX O2 agent service to Docker Compose stack]:
  Added the missing dxo2 service and apmia_data named volume to
  docker-compose.yml so the PHP probe and BPA WebServer Plugin are injected
  in local development the same way they are in Kubernetes.

  docker-compose.yml:
  - New dxo2 service (build: ./src/dx-o2-agents, pull_policy: never).
    Mounts apmia_data:/opt/apmia read-write so Docker's volume-init copies
    /opt/apmia from the image into the named volume on first start — the
    Compose equivalent of the dxo2-init Kubernetes initContainer.
  - phpfpm: added apmia_data:/opt/apmia:ro volume mount; added
    APMIA_PHP_COLLECTOR_HOST=dxo2, APMIA_PHP_COLLECTOR_PORT, APMIA_APP_NAME
    env vars; added depends_on dxo2 (condition: service_started).
  - nginx: added apmia_data:/opt/apmia:ro volume mount; added
    APMIA_BTL_HOST=dxo2, APMIA_BTL_PORT env vars; added depends_on dxo2.
  - Added apmia_data named volume to the volumes block.
  Note: In Compose, services communicate by service name (not 127.0.0.1
  as in a Kubernetes pod), so IPC host vars are set to 'dxo2', not
  127.0.0.1.  CLAUDE.md Docker Compose section updated accordingly.

  CLAUDE.md:
  - Docker Compose notes: removed "No DX O2 agent in the Compose stack"
    (now outdated); replaced with accurate description of dxo2 service and
    Compose-vs-Kubernetes networking difference.

