2026-06-11 @ 11:22  Registry credentials via Kubernetes ServiceAccount

  New files:
  - helm/php-demo/templates/serviceaccount.yaml
      Dedicated ServiceAccount for the pod with automountServiceAccountToken
      set to false.  imagePullSecrets is conditionally set to the registry
      pull secret when credentials are provided.
  - helm/php-demo/templates/registry-secret.yaml
      kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson Secret built from imageCredentials.*
      values.  Only rendered when username and password are both non-empty,
      keeping the chart usable against public registries without credentials.

  Modified files:
  - helm/php-demo/templates/_helpers.tpl
      Added php-demo.registrySecretName helper and php-demo.dockerconfigjson
      helper that encodes base64(<username>:<password>) into the auth field.
  - helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml
      Replaced pod-level imagePullSecrets block with serviceAccountName
      referencing the new ServiceAccount.  Pull credentials are now inherited
      automatically by the kubelet for all three containers.
  - helm/php-demo/values.yaml
      Replaced imagePullSecrets: [] with imageCredentials stanza
      (registry / username / password, all empty by default).
  - scripts/deploy.sh
      Added imageCredentials block (sourced from .config) to the generated
      values.local.yaml so credentials reach Helm at deploy time.
  - scripts/push.sh
      Fixed docker login: replaced echo with printf '%s' when piping the
      password to --password-stdin.  echo appends a trailing newline that
      some registry daemons reject as an invalid credential.

